Xing Han was born in Anhui province, China. He received his BS degree from Anhui Normal University in 2013. After then, he joined the research group of Prof. Yong Cui at Shanghai Jiao Tong University and obtained his PhD degree in 2019. His research interest focuses on design and synthesis of crystalline porous materials.
Yan Liu received her BS degree in applied chemistry in 2006 and PhD in chemistry in 2011 from Shanghai Jiao Tong University She conducted postdoctoral research at the University of North Carolina (2011–2013). She joined the Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2014, where she is now a professor of chemistry. Her research interest focuses on supramolecular chemistry and coordination chemistry.
Haiyang Li obtained his BS in chemistry in 2011 and received his PhD degree in inorganic chemistry in 2017 from Zhengzhou University under the supervision of Prof. Thomas C. W. Mak and Prof. Shuang-Quan Zang in 2017. After then, he joined the college of chemistry of Zhengzhou University in 2017. His current research focuses on the design and synthesis of functional porous framework material.
Yong Cui received his PhD in physical chemistry in 1999 from Fujian Institute of Research on the Structure of Matter, CAS. He conducted postdoctoral research at University of Science and Technology of China, University of North Carolina-Chapel Hill and University of Chicago from 1999 to 2005. He joined the Shanghai Jiao Tong University in 2005, where he is now a chair professor of chemistry. His research interest focuses on the fields of porous materials, asymmetric catalysis, chiral separation and chiral optics.
This work was financially supported by the National Science Foundation of China (Grants 21431004, 21620102001, 21875136 and 91856204), the National Key Basic Research Program of China (Grant 2016YFA0203400), the Key Project of Basic Research of Shanghai (17JC1403100 and 18JC1413200), the Shanghai Rising-Star Program (19QA1404300), the postdoctoral innovative talent support program (BX20190195), and the China postdoctoral science foundation (2019M661483).
