## Entry for the Table of Contents
The development of metal-covalent organic frameworks (MCOFs) hold high promise in addressing the shortcomings of metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) and covalent organic frameworks (COFs), which exhibits a balanced mix of crystallinity, porosity, stability, tunability, and functionality. This Minireview summarizes the recent progress of MCOFs regarding the design strategy, synthesis, structural characterization, and their cutting-edge applications.
